ZapIME VoiceKey integration: source and permission boundaries

ZapIME-authored adapter code and modifications are GPL-3.0-only. The full text
is in GPL-3.0.txt. This declaration does not relicense upstream VoiceKey code.

Upstream source: https://github.com/J3n5en/voicekey
Pinned revision: 3ba017826eef7fac405198510b03859eb5b6c8c4
Authors: J3n5en and the contributors recorded in that pinned repository.
The pristine source remains in vendor/voicekey. Local adapted files retain
source/authorship notices and their relationship to that fixed revision.

On 2026-11-06 the ZapIME project owner explicitly confirmed that the VoiceKey
author agrees to incorporation of the author's source in ZapIME. The project
uses that confirmation for this integration work; a standardized public
upstream license or independently supplied distribution terms have not been
recorded. Do not treat this notice as a grant of unrestricted redistribution
rights or as a statement that all upstream source is GPL licensed. Broader
binary distribution remains subject to documenting the relevant terms.

The author's source permission does not cover third-party acoustic model
weights, proprietary libraries, vendor services, extracted credentials or
non-public protocols. Those rights require independent verification. No
third-party VoiceKey model weights or vendor service credentials are bundled
by this integration. ZapIME compiles only the documented offline adapter
scope; importing the complete source submodule does not enable its services.
